{"company":{"id":"notion","name":"Notion","accent":"#ffffff","asset":"page blocks","verb":"open a page"},"nodes":[{"id":"client","title":"Desktop / phone / web","kind":"client","blurb":"Upload, download, sync.","depth":0,"story":"This is the Notion app on your phone or laptop. Tapping open a page starts here. The app does not hold the whole product — it only starts the request."},{"id":"api","title":"Control API","kind":"api","blurb":"Metadata: names, sharing, versions.","depth":1,"story":"Think of this as Notion’s front desk. The app asks it for “what’s allowed / what’s next,” not for huge page blocks. It routes, limits traffic, and hides internal stores."},{"id":"cdn","title":"CDN","kind":"cdn","blurb":"Downloads of popular public files.","depth":1,"story":"On Notion, bulky page blocks are copied around the world. Play/browse should hit a nearby copy. If that copy is missing, a miss goes back to origin."},{"id":"auth","title":"Identity + ACL","kind":"auth","blurb":"Who can read this path.","depth":2,"story":"Before Notion shows anything private, it checks who you are (account, session, device). A CDN copy of a file is not the same as being logged in."},{"id":"meta","title":"Metadata service","kind":"service","blurb":"Tree of folders and pointers.","depth":2,"story":"Folder names, sharing, versions. The tree of files — not the file bytes."},{"id":"block","title":"Block / chunk service","kind":"service","blurb":"File split into chunks.","depth":2,"story":"Notion splits a large upload into chunks so a flaky wifi can retry a piece, not the whole file."},{"id":"dedup","title":"Dedup / delta","kind":"service","blurb":"Skip bytes you already stored.","depth":3,"story":"If that chunk was already stored (same photo, same backup), skip shipping it again."},{"id":"cache","title":"Metadata cache","kind":"cache","blurb":"Hot folder listings.","depth":3,"story":"The same questions get asked thousands of times (session, “is this still available?”). Notion keeps those answers in fast memory so the main database is not hit every time."},{"id":"metadb","title":"Metadata DB","kind":"db","blurb":"Namespace, not file bytes.","depth":4,"story":"The official map of titles and relationships. Separate from your personal history and from the video warehouse."},{"id":"blob","title":"Chunk store","kind":"blob","blurb":"Immutable blocks across machines.","depth":4,"story":"The warehouse for large page blocks. Cheap to store, not great for “show my last 20 items.” Notion points at these files from the records database."},{"id":"queue","title":"Index / virus queue","kind":"queue","blurb":"Scan and thumbnail offline.","depth":5,"story":"Slow leftover work (encode, notify, payout) waits here after you already succeeded at open a page. The tap can return; workers finish later."},{"id":"workers","title":"Processors","kind":"workers","blurb":"Preview, search index, AV scan.","depth":5,"story":"Background helpers at Notion. They retry if something fails. They are not sitting on the button you just pressed."},{"id":"sync","title":"Notification / sync","kind":"workers","blurb":"Other devices pull changes.","depth":6,"story":"Your other devices hear “there is a new version.” They pull; the upload already succeeded."},{"id":"search","title":"Content search","kind":"service","blurb":"Optional: find inside files.","depth":6,"story":"Find inside files or posts. That is an index, not the warehouse itself."},{"id":"block-graph","title":"Block graph","kind":"service","blurb":"Builds pages from reusable blocks and resolves nested references.","depth":6,"story":"Builds pages from reusable blocks and resolves nested references."}],"edges":[{"from":"client","to":"api","label":"names / share"},{"from":"client","to":"cdn","label":"download"},{"from":"api","to":"auth","label":"ACL"},{"from":"api","to":"meta","label":"folder tree"},{"from":"client","to":"block","label":"upload chunks"},{"from":"block","to":"dedup","label":"skip known bytes"},{"from":"block","to":"blob","label":"store chunks"},{"from":"meta","to":"cache","label":"hot listings"},{"from":"meta","to":"metadb","label":"namespace"},{"from":"meta","to":"queue","label":"scan later"},{"from":"queue","to":"workers","label":"preview / AV"},{"from":"workers","to":"search","label":"index text"},{"from":"meta","to":"sync","label":"other devices"},{"from":"cdn","to":"blob","label":"cache miss"},{"from":"workers","to":"block-graph","label":"index blocks"}],"stages":[{"i":0,"blurb":"Renaming a file is an API call. Downloading a popular file often hits a nearby CDN.","unlockNodeIds":["client","api","cdn"],"unlockEdgeIds":["client->api","client->cdn","api->auth","api->meta","client->block","cdn->blob"]},{"i":1,"blurb":"Permissions live with the folder names. The file itself is uploaded in chunks on a separate path.","unlockNodeIds":["auth","meta","block"],"unlockEdgeIds":["api->auth","api->meta","client->block","block->dedup","block->blob","meta->cache","meta->metadb","meta->queue","meta->sync"]},{"i":2,"blurb":"Skip bytes you already stored. Folder lists you open all day sit in a cache.","unlockNodeIds":["dedup","cache"],"unlockEdgeIds":["block->dedup","meta->cache"]},{"i":3,"blurb":"Names and sharing rules in a database; the actual chunks in object storage.","unlockNodeIds":["metadb","blob"],"unlockEdgeIds":["block->blob","meta->metadb","cdn->blob"]},{"i":4,"blurb":"Virus scan and previews happen after upload succeeds, so the app can say “saved” quickly.","unlockNodeIds":["queue","workers"],"unlockEdgeIds":["meta->queue","queue->workers","workers->search","workers->block-graph"]},{"i":5,"blurb":"Other devices get told there is a new version. Search is an index, not the file warehouse.","unlockNodeIds":["sync","search","block-graph"],"unlockEdgeIds":["workers->search","meta->sync"]}],"questions":[{"id":"notion-0-bytes-vs-control-0-0","stage":0,"tid":"bytes-vs-control","variant":0,"correct":"split-paths","distractors":["all-cdn","all-api","all-db"],"seed":2626857722},{"id":"notion-0-bytes-vs